WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.240
I'm talking really fast because I'm trying to be like John Green even though I'm not John Green,

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.380
which is something you probably noticed.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.560
I'm also trying not to blink and I'm going down in pitch right before my jump cuts.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:11.400
Also, Hank, I'm trying to make the puff level on my hair higher, but I don't have very much,

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.580
and I'm afraid if I keep doing this, I'll go bald permanently.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.340
Yes, I realize John Green wears glasses, but if I put on my glasses, I'll look exactly like Vsauce.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:21.300
And many of you nerdfighters right now are saying to yourself, "He's not Vsauce?" No, I'm not Vsauce.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:22.020
So who am I?

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:22.520
Hi. [sigh]

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:27.240
I'm Craig Wheezy Waiter. That's my real last name, according to John's previous video.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.640
"And Craig Wheezy Waiter, which is his real last name."

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.200
I'm responsible for that beard over there on the Vlogbrothers channel, but in all other regards,

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.420
I'm not responsible, at all. That's why I make clones do my chores.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:37.440
Clone: "Hi."

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:38.940
Get back to work, clone.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:43.800
So why am I here and when do I leave, many of you are asking. Well, you're not asking- You're not saying "I",

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:48.540
you're saying "you", so why am you here and when do you leave? Well, substitute am for are.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:52.960
Because John had a baby. Well, Sarah had the baby. John helped.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.800
They brought Alice Green into the world. That picture is just a random baby. That is not their baby.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:00.660
That might be a boy baby. Uh, there. There we go.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:06.340
I can also try to approximate the sound of the baby for you. [crying baby noises]

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:09.280
[coughing] Only going to do that once.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.640
The reason that I'm so good at impersonating a baby is because of your most recent video, Hank.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.020
"How to be a Baby Properly." I actually wrote down your list about how to be a baby, Hank,

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:17.120
to make sure I got it right.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.160
So here's your list, if I understand it correctly: You're stuck in the world, get used to it.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:20.800
Cry.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.480
Sleep 2.5 hours at a time.

00:01:22.480 --> 00:01:23.780
Put stuff in your mouth.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:25.100
Cry all the time, again.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:26.380
And, try to be cute.

00:01:26.380 --> 00:01:32.500
That is exactly what I did in college. I failed at the last one. Anyway, Hank and John, it is an honor to be on your

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:36.420
channel and once I learned I was going to be on your channel, I knew I had to step up my game

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.260
because I normally do stuff like this:

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:39.580
"Here's me with my shirt off."

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:40.860
I'm not proud of it.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.460
I am proud of it, but I'm ashamed that I'm proud of it.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:46.340
So I needed some practice interacting with Nerdfighters before I made this video.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:47.760
Therefore, I made a nerdfighter clone.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.620
Nerdfighter clone, are you there?

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:51.120
"Yes."

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:52.160
Why didn't you say anything?

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.020
"You didn't ask. I was just being polite."

00:01:54.020 --> 00:01:55.760
You just never forget to be awesome, do you?

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:56.680
"DFTBA"

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.880
Oh hey, listen, I think I saw some worldsuck in the bathroom. Do you think you can go decrease it?

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:01.600
With a mop?

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:02.540
Thank you.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:03.280
"Yes."

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:07.720
Anyway, nerdighter clone didn't help because every time I talked to him, I just kept getting jealous by how

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:11.260
awesome he didn't forget to be. So I just decided to do a bunch of things that John Green does,

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:15.300
like Question Tuesday, the day I answer fake questions that I just made up, but I assume that you are wondering,

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:19.380
but I'm not going to answer real questions because I'm not a Vlogbrother and I'd probably answer inaccurately.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.260
"When's John coming back?"

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.880
I'm not sure, but it's going to be a bunch of weeks and different people are going to host in his place each week

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:24.780
"Why's your name Wheezy Waiter?"

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.120
My name is Wheezy Waiter because I have asthma and I used to be a waiter.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:29.260
"Do you hate Vsauce because he looks so much like you?"

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:33.100
No, we're friends. Ha. Such good friends.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:34.820
No, for real, we are friends.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:35.640
"Who the eff is Hank?"

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:39.760
Hank is a large flippered marine mammal found in the Arctic Ocean and Hank may also refer to the movement

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:40.580
that a Hank makes.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:45.720
[Claps] See? I'm hanking right now. Hank you very much.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:47.340
I'm a dork.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.300
"Will you do Sharpie face?"

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:54.020
Oh, I don't have any Sharpies. But I do have crackers, so I will smash one my forehead.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:59.460
Yeah, that'll be my thing now. Then I'll eat it too.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:03.800
That was an easy target to hit, if you know what I mean. Oh ho ho, I'm balding. It's sad.

00:03:03.980 --> 00:03:08.360
What else does John Green do? Thoughts from places. Okay, how about my office? Here goes:

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:12.700
Often, when one thinks of an office, feelings such as confinement and separation come to mind,

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:17.780
which is why I very deliberately located my office in this open corner of my girlfriend's and my abode.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:22.040
Notice the windows lining the periphery. One can even discover infinity in this locale.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:25.500
No longer is there separation, but connection to everything.

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:30.380
What else? Ah, something literary. The work of Oscar Wilde often contains critique of social issues,

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:37.120
like false manners, hypocrisy, fraudulent identities, and nowhere is it more exemplary than in this passage: [clears throat]

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:41.140
"Whizz, whizz went the Catherine wheel, as she spun round and round."

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.380
Probably should have planned that out a little better.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.200
Wow, he's often in an airport, I'll go to the airport.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:47.140
No, I don't feel like going to the airport.

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:50.180
Oh, you know what else? He's also not in an airport very often. I'll do that instead.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:53.080
Here I am. Ah, this is one of my favorite not-airports.

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:54.420
Hank, I'll see you on Friday.

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:55.620
And, DFTBA.

